      "message": "So, to reformulate what I think the approach is:\n\n* you take a big-endian encoding of each field (the same encoding as the \"mathematical\" encoding where the MSB comes first)\n* you add these bits together to a bigger number, start starting with the _last_ field\n* finally, you take this number and encode it as little- or big-endian as necessary.\n\nThat should match what I get above and what you\u0027ve documented.\n\nSo if we have\n\n```\npacket Foo {\n  a: 1,\n  b: 2,\n  c: 5,\n}\n```\n\nthen you would still put the bits into a single byte like this:\n\n```\nc4 c3 c2 c1 c0 b1 b0 a0\n```\n\nThat would be the encoding in both little- and big-endian, right?",
